    {
      "id": "p0120-b005",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The English phrase \"Sunday best\" refers to the kind of nice, formal clothing one is expected to wear to church on Sundays. Only about 1% of the Japanese population is Christian, so a literal translation of \"Sunday best\" wouldn't make much sense, and the made-up \"Tuesday pretty-good\" would make even less sense.",
        "raw": "The English phrase \"Sunday best\" refers to the kind of nice, formal clothing\none is expected to wear to church on Sundays. Only about 1% of the\nJapanese population is Christian, so a literal translation of \"Sunday best\"\nwouldn't make much sense, and the made-up \"Tuesday pretty-good\" would\nmake even less sense.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29291586,
          0.35055,
          0.87672634,
          0.43317857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29046588,
          0.34983571,
          0.90393136,
          0.43425
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          13,
          14,
          15,
          16,
          17
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英语短语“Sunday best”指的是星期日上教堂时应该穿的漂亮正装。日本人口中只有约1%是基督徒，因此直译“Sunday best”很难让人明白，自造的“Tuesday pretty-good”就更难懂了。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
